# Gate of the ipu4-patches / ipu4 leg (tools/tests/ipu6/ladder.sh): the
# upstreamable driver (Ruslan's tree + patches/ipu6-ipu4/) under the IPU4
# QEMU model. Owned by the IPU4 port (tools/notes/ipu6-ipu4-plan.md); each
# PR in its sequence enables at least one more test.
#
# One test name per line; '#' starts a comment. Every known test runs on
# every PR, but only the tests listed here fail the job; run
# `tools/tests/ipu6/ladder.sh --list` for the names.

# Static tests (plan PR 3).
series-applies
build
checkpatch

# Guest kernel + initramfs boot under the QEMU IPU4 model (plan PR 4).
vm-boot

# virt-sensor + intel-ipu6* load/unload, 5a88 still unbound (plan PR 5).
module-load

# new_id bind of 5a88 identifies IPU4 (plan PR 6, first kernel patch).
probe-identify

# ISYS/PSYS power-up through the IPU4 buttress controls (plan PR 7).
probe-buttress

# PSYS MMU init writes the IPU4 stream tables seen on silicon (plan PR 8).
probe-mmu

# Forced ISYS runtime resume: ISYS MMU, TSC sync and UNISPART interrupt
# setup write what silicon writes (plan PR 9).
isys-irq

# The ISYS firmware opens over IPU4's SysCom layout and answers the first
# STREAM_OPEN; the SysCom writes match silicon's (plan PR 11).
fw-open

# VIDIOC_STREAMON succeeds through the IPU4 CSI-2 receiver (no PHY, no
# iWake); receiver and iWake writes match silicon's stream (plan PR 12).
stream-on

# The captured frame holds the QEMU model's test pattern (plan PR 12).
stream-pattern

# A CSI-2 frame start interrupt arrives on port 0; the CSI2PART/CSI2S2M
# interrupt setup and teardown match silicon's stream (plan PR 13).
csi2-sof-irq

# ISYS runtime resume incl. the TSC sync handshake (gated with the IPU6
# variant's V12).
isys-resume
